<title>Solitary Renal Cyst: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0648-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Simple cyst (no septa) or minimally complex cyst (1 or 2 hairline thin septa) on initial imaging (usually ultrasound)?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No (more complex cyst)</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Symptomatic?</label>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>No follow-up required.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>NSAIDs or acetaminophen for pain; consider aspiration with or without sclerosants, or surgical decortication (open or laparoscopic).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Bosniak category on CT&#x002F;MRI.</label>
<path target="cell-2">Bosniak I or II</path>
<path target="cell-6">Bosniak IIF</path>
<path target="cell-7">Bosniak III or IV</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Follow-up with additional imaging.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Surgical referral.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
